WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:08.259
AI-assisted secure code review should fit
into existing engineering workflows.

2
00:00:08.339 --> 00:00:15.086
In pull requests, it can help summarize
the security-relevant change,

3
00:00:15.166 --> 00:00:21.126
generate review questions, compare the
change to a checklist,

4
00:00:21.206 --> 00:00:24.917
or draft a finding for a human reviewer.

5
00:00:24.997 --> 00:00:31.745
For larger reviews, it can help organize
notes by component, risk area,

6
00:00:31.825 --> 00:00:33.174
and evidence.

7
00:00:33.254 --> 00:00:37.640
The output should support the review
process,

8
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:44.917
not create a second undocumented process
that developers cannot inspect or

9
00:00:44.997 --> 00:00:46.121
challenge.

10
00:00:46.201 --> 00:00:52.274
AI also pairs well with SAST and SCA
results when used carefully.

11
00:00:52.354 --> 00:00:59.663
It can group similar findings, explain a
tool result, suggest likely owners,

12
00:00:59.743 --> 00:01:02.779
or propose verification steps.

13
00:01:02.859 --> 00:01:06.570
But scanner output still needs triage,

14
00:01:06.650 --> 00:01:12.273
and AI summaries can accidentally hide
important details.

15
00:01:12.353 --> 00:01:19.437
Keep links to original findings, affected
files, versions, and evidence.

16
00:01:19.517 --> 00:01:26.714
Ticketing should distinguish verified
vulnerabilities from hypotheses,

17
00:01:26.794 --> 00:01:32.642
accepted risk, false positives, and
backlog hardening work.

18
00:01:32.722 --> 00:01:37.445
Governance protects both the code and the
review.

19
00:01:37.525 --> 00:01:44.385
Privacy controls should prevent secrets,
credentials, customer data,

20
00:01:44.465 --> 00:01:52.336
and sensitive business logic from being
sent to tools that are not approved for that

21
00:01:52.416 --> 00:01:52.978
data.

22
00:01:53.058 --> 00:02:00.818
Evidence notes should be clear enough for
audit and repeatable enough for another

23
00:02:00.898 --> 00:02:03.259
reviewer to understand.

24
00:02:03.339 --> 00:02:09.637
Developers should receive practical,
respectful explanations.

25
00:02:09.717 --> 00:02:14.215
Human approval remains required before
merge,

26
00:02:14.295 --> 00:02:18.455
especially for AI-generated remediation.

27
00:02:18.535 --> 00:02:25.620
A mature workflow makes AI assistance
visible, bounded, and accountable.
